From 0f872a5745378443ec5df2afc79f2ba562ba2849 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:47:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(connected-accounts): automated Mastodon posts for
 collectives

Part of opencollective/opencollective#7138: make the Fediverse a first
class citizen for automated announcements, replacing what the removed
Twitter integration used to do.

- Add a `MicrobloggingService` interface (server/lib/microblogging) and
  its Mastodon implementation. Collectives connect an account with an
  access token from their Mastodon server, stored encrypted in a
  `mastodon` ConnectedAccount. All requests go through the webhook SSRF
  protections (pinned DNS, no private addresses, no redirects).
- Activity-to-post pipeline, called by the notifications dispatcher on
  `collective.member.created`: thank new financial contributors (with
  a mention when their profile links a Mastodon account, never for
  incognito contributors) and celebrate contributor milestones.
- Monthly CRON job posting the stats of the previous month, threaded
  with the previous report.
- Each post type can be toggled per account. Posts are rate limited,
  deduplicated with Idempotency-Key and fit the server's character
  limit. Accounts whose token was revoked are flagged for reconnection.
- GraphQL: `createConnectedAccount` accepts `service: mastodon` with
  `instanceUrl`, new `editConnectedAccountPostSettings` mutation,
  `ConnectedAccount.username` and post settings for admins.
- Everything is behind the `MICROBLOGGING_POSTS` feature flag (off by
  default).
